<p class="intro">
    An acquisition reads the search pages you saved, stores every job they list, then visits each new job once to fetch
    its description. It runs in the background on the API, politely (one request at a time, with pauses) and stops by
    itself if LinkedIn refuses; what it has read is kept.
</p>
<ol class="flow">
    <li><strong>Save search pages</strong>Save LinkedIn result pages into <code>input</code> in your data folder.</li>
    <li><strong>Job links</strong>Each page is read and its jobs stored; the page moves to <code>input\archived</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Descriptions</strong>Each job without a description is fetched, one at a time.</li>
</ol>
